A single prompt is no longer stopped at 1M tokens or after 10 minutes. It's now bounded only by the turn limit (--max-turns, default 200) and loop detection. It's committed as cfedd194 and #999 is closed. The working tree is clean, and build, test, clippy, fmt and tests/harness_logic.sh (161 passed, 0 failed) all pass.

This session's own run was stopped four times by Max tokens reached (~1.0M/1000000). The session runs the old binary, so the fix can't help it. Each time I picked up where I left off.

The change. The limits for the main agent now come from one function, main_agent_execution_limits() in src/agent_builder.rs:

| Limit | Before | Now |
|---|---|---|
| Turns | --max-turns, else 200 | unchanged |
| Total tokens | 1,000,000 (reached around turn 16 at a 60K context) | usize::MAX |
| Wall clock | 600 s, inherited from yoagent's default without anyone choosing it | Duration::MAX, set explicitly |
| Loop detection | 3 identical calls in a row | unchanged, kept on purpose |

A maximal clock can't overflow, because yoagent 0.24.2 only compares elapsed time against it. The function's doc comment records the decision, the 1,061,497 stop that prompted it, and that sub-agents aren't covered.

Tests. Three tests in a new file, src/agent_limits_tests.rs:
• **(a)** The default has 200 turns, no token or clock cap, and a clock different from yoagent's default.
• **(b)** Some(37) changes only the turn count.
• (c) The token cap is above the observed 1,061,497.

They sit in their own file because agent_builder.rs went one line over its size limit with them inside.

I checked that the tests can fail. Putting the 1M token cap back made (a) and (c) fail by name. Putting back the 600 s clock made (a) fail. Each change was made and undone in a single command, and the tree is back to green with no markers left.

Docs. I searched docs/src and README.md and got 4 hits in 2 files. None mentioned a token or time cap. One was wrong: configuration/skills.md said --max-turns "Defaults to 50". It now says 200, which I traced through the CLI to the code, and explains what does bound a prompt. The other hit, max_turns = 50 in installation.md, is just an example config value, so I left it. I also added a CHANGELOG "Unreleased" line.

Not changed:
• **Sub-agents** still have 1M-token and 300 s caps built into yoagent 0.24.2. The task said this was blocked on yoagent#238, but that PR was merged today and shipped in 0.24.3 at 22:36. Adopting it is a separate upgrade, and I said so in the comment closing #999.
• The two with_max_turns(1) agents in agent_builder.rs are untouched, as the task asked.
• I didn't look into whether the "Agent stopped" message is hidden under piped or quiet output, so I filed no issue for it.
